      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** If `fp_sensor_get_info` fails or `num_types` is out of bounds, this function currently executes an early `return;` instead of `goto error_exit;`. \n\nWhile this might be harmless if `populate_cache` is only ever called once at startup, it\u0027s safer and more consistent to invalidate the cache (fill with zeros) on *any* failure to prevent the cache from containing stale or partially uninitialized data. \n\nConsider changing these early returns to `goto error_exit;`:\n```cpp\n\tif (fp_sensor_get_info(info, buffer.size()) \u003c 0) {\n\t\tCPRINTS(\"Error: Failed to get fingerprint sensor info.\");\n\t\tgoto error_exit;\n\t}\n\n\tconst uint8_t num_types \u003d info-\u003esensor_info.num_capture_types;\n\n\tif (num_types \u003e frame_params_.size()) {\n\t\tCPRINTS(\"ERROR - EC returned %u types, max supported is %zu.\",\n\t\t\tnum_types, frame_params_.size());\n\t\tgoto error_exit;\n\t}\n```\n[🔗](http://go/tj/cns/gg-d/home/tomhughes@google.com/review_trajectories/cl8372808_05396d31-ec1e-40de-9b4b-e9be47d4713c.pb)",
