      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Security / Bounds Validation (Blocking):** The validation checks that `size` and `offset` individually do not exceed `max_image_buffer_bytes`. However, as established in the previous CL review, the image payload resides at `[offset, offset + size)`. This means the combined footprint (`offset + size`) must not exceed the physical buffer capacity.\n\nFor example, if `max_image_buffer_bytes` is 1500, `offset` is 1000, and `size` is 1000, both individual checks pass, but the total required capacity is 2000, which risks an out-of-bounds read later. Furthermore, if `offset + size` wraps around (integer overflow), it could bypass a simple addition check.\n\nPlease replace both checks with a unified footprint check that also prevents overflow:\n```cpp\n\t\tif (offset \u003e max_image_buffer_bytes ||\n\t\t    max_image_buffer_bytes - offset \u003c size) {\n\t\t\tCPRINTS(\"Error: Type %u payload [offset %u, size %u] exceeds max buffer (%u).\",\n\t\t\t\ttype, offset, size, max_image_buffer_bytes);\n\t\t\tgoto error_exit;\n\t\t}\n```\n[🔗](http://go/tj/cns/gg-d/home/tomhughes@google.com/review_trajectories/cl8372808_05396d31-ec1e-40de-9b4b-e9be47d4713c.pb)",
